<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Drawn size of the app icon widget's icon. Deliberately a fixed size centred in the cell rather than
      match_parent: launcher cells are much larger than an app icon, so filling the cell is exactly
      what made the widget read as oversized next to real icons. Overridden at runtime from GumshoosConfig, so this is
      only the initial value — tune it from the app's App icon widget screen instead.
    -->
    <dimen name="widget_icon_size">46dp</dimen>

    <!--
      Wide search bar metrics. Referenced from widget_search_bar.xml and, via dimensionResource,
      from the settings preview — one source, so the preview can't quietly disagree with the widget
      about how much room the logo takes or how far the content sits from the edge.
    -->
    <dimen name="widget_bar_inset">18dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="widget_bar_gap">12dp</dimen>
    <!--
      Between the temperature and its condition mark, which are one reading rather than two slots.
      The 12dp above is what separates *different* actions, and at that width the mark read as its
      own thing sitting next to the number instead of belonging to it.

      Applied only as a runtime action — the layout gives every slot view the standard gap, and this
      overrides it for the one view that is sharing a slot rather than occupying its own.
    -->
    <dimen name="widget_bar_pair_gap">6dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="widget_bar_logo_size">22dp</dimen>
    <!--
      A dp under the logo, deliberately: the three action marks sit together and read heavy at the
      logo's size.

      Every action mark inks its whole canvas, so this is the size they are actually drawn at, less
      whatever optical trim WidgetAction.iconScale applies. Lens did not always: it shipped with a
      12.5% transparent margin from Google's export, so fitCenter gave it 16.5dp here while Gemini
      and the mic got the full 22dp, and the three looked mismatched however this number was set.
      Cropping the viewBox in design/icons/ic_provider_lens.svg is what fixed it. Measure a new mark
      the same way before adding it — a margin of its own comes off this size silently, and this is
      the one thing that cannot be corrected from here.
    -->
    <dimen name="widget_bar_action_size">21dp</dimen>
    <!--
      The date and weather readouts, and the same size as the hint beside them.

      Pushed at runtime by setTextViewTextSize, and that is not belt and braces. A launcher
      reuses the view hierarchy it already inflated when the layout id is unchanged — RemoteViews
      actions are re-applied, but an attribute that lives only in XML is not, so editing this number
      alone leaves every already-placed widget at the old size until the launcher happens to
      re-inflate. The same class of staleness as the drawable ids, and the same remedy: make it an
      action rather than something the launcher has to have noticed.
    -->
    <dimen name="widget_bar_slot_text">14sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="widget_bar_hint_text">16sp</dimen>

</resources>
